# Local Branch Workflow

This repo uses a local `working` branch that intentionally carries local-only setup commits.

- Treat any commit whose subject starts with `local:` as local-only.
- Always treat the existing commit with subject `claude init` as local-only too.
- Local-only commits should stay on `working` and should not be included in upstream PR branches.
- When preparing a PR branch, branch from `ups/main` and cherry-pick only non-local commits from `working`.
- When syncing `working` with `ups/main`, preserve the local-only commits on top.
- Prefer keeping local-only setup commits squashed/rebased near the top of `working` and using the `local:` prefix for new ones.
- Do not rewrite or drop local-only commits unless the user explicitly asks.
